# config/claude-shaped-store - Claude credential stores this home paces at a
# limit-reset edge. One absolute path per line; '#' comments and blank lines are
# ignored. An absent file means no store is shaped and every Claude launch is
# released unchanged.
#
# The path is the store a launch actually bills, which is what
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR selects for that pane (the default store is ~/.claude).
# Copy this file to config/claude-shaped-store and list only the stores you
# want paced - typically a shared work subscription, not your personal one.
#
# See docs/configuration.md "Claude release shaping" for the full contract and
# bin/fm-claude-admission.sh --help for the commands.

/home/example/.claude-work
